From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:18:37 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] media: venus: venc: Use CAVLC with the Baseline profiles

CABAC is not part of the H.264 Baseline and Constrained Baseline
profiles, but the encoder passes the entropy mode control on to the
firmware whatever the profile. Given CABAC with the Baseline profile,
the msm8996 firmware (VIDEO.VE.4.4-00060) fails fatally on the first
frame, with an Err_Fatal at venus_venc_host_driver.c:5844 in its SFR
message, and the session and the core have to be recovered.

Send CAVLC with those profiles, like the 8x8 transform is only enabled
with the High profiles.

Tested on a Samsung Galaxy Tab S3 (msm8996): GStreamer's v4l2h264enc
asked for CABAC negotiates the Baseline profile and now encodes with
CAVLC instead of crashing the firmware; with the Main profile the
stream uses CABAC.

Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
index 7760f56534..ea87b0f432 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
@@ -735,6 +735,10 @@ static int venc_set_properties(struct venus_inst *inst)
 		entropy.entropy_mode = venc_v4l2_to_hfi(
 					  V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_H264_ENTROPY_MODE,
 					  ctr->h264_entropy_mode);
+		/* CABAC is not part of the Baseline profiles */
+		if (ctr->profile.h264 == V4L2_MPEG_VIDEO_H264_PROFILE_BASELINE ||
+		    ctr->profile.h264 == V4L2_MPEG_VIDEO_H264_PROFILE_CONSTRAINED_BASELINE)
+			entropy.entropy_mode = HFI_H264_ENTROPY_CAVLC;
 		entropy.cabac_model = HFI_H264_CABAC_MODEL_0;
 
 		ret = hfi_session_set_property(inst, ptype, &entropy);
